  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "CONVERT evaluates linear units via a three-store x87 PC64 chain, treats bar as #N/A, and uses direct affine temperature pairs",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20228 and 20527, CONVERT(number, from_unit, to_unit) evaluates supported linear categories via three x87 PC64 operations each stored to binary64 before the next: RN53(RN64(RN53(RN64(number * from_factor)) / to_factor) * decimal_prefix_delta), where decimal_prefix_delta is the single binary64 power 10^(from_exp - to_exp) rather than a quotient of prefix factors; length factors use exact integer angstroms, pressure stores independent reciprocals of units-per-pascal while rejecting bar with #N/A, and K/C/F use six direct affine formulas. Matches 33,972/33,972 full-bank and 120/120 pinned CONVERT rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 33,972 full-bank and 120 pinned CONVERT rows in Excel 16.0 build 20228 (witnesses/CONVERT.json, W109_CONVERT_IDENTIFICATION_20260809.md) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 50).",
